---
/**
 * Terms of use.
 *
 * The parts that matter here are the disclaimer and the licensing, because this
 * site publishes other people's data under their licences and its own coding
 * under ours, and a reader needs to know which is which before reusing anything.
 */
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const updated = "13 September 2026";
---

<Base
  title="Terms"
  description="Terms of use: no advice, no warranty, licensing of material published here and of material reproduced from third parties."
  cites={[]}
>
  <section class="section section--open">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="masthead">
        <h1>Terms</h1>
        <p class="masthead__meta mono">Last updated {updated}</p>
      </div>

      <div class="doc">
        <p class="lede">
          Nothing published on this site is legal, financial, investment or professional advice.
        </p>

        <h2>No advice</h2>
        <p>
          The AI Law and Policy Index is a reading of public instruments at a stated review date.
          It does not account for individual circumstances, it is not a compliance product, and
          qualified practitioners may code entries differently. Obtain advice from a practitioner
          qualified in the relevant jurisdiction before relying on it.
        </p>
        <p>
          Governance readiness scores record the machinery a jurisdiction has. They are not an
          assessment of the quality of its rules or of their enforcement.
        </p>

        <h2>No warranty</h2>
        <p>
          The site is provided as is, without warranty of any kind. Figures are reproduced from
          third-party datasets that carry their own errors, revisions and limitations, and
          processing here may introduce further errors. Each figure carries its source, licence and
          retrieval date so that it can be verified against the original.
        </p>
        <p>
          To the extent the law allows, we accept no liability for any loss arising from use of
          this site or reliance on anything published here. Nothing in these terms limits rights
          you have under the Australian Consumer Law or equivalent legislation that cannot be
          excluded.
        </p>

        <h2>Material published under our licence</h2>
        <p>
          The site's code, its written explanations and the four datasets compiled here are
          licensed <a href="https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT">MIT</a>. Reuse, modification and
          commercial use are permitted, subject to retention of the copyright notice.
        </p>
        <p>
          The four datasets are the
          <a href="/methodology/governance-readiness/">AI Governance Readiness Index</a>, the
          <a href="/policy/">AI Law and Policy Index</a>, the
          <a href="/alignment/#frameworks">Frontier Safety Framework Index</a> and the
          <a href="/capability/#thresholds">Compute Threshold Index</a>. Each is compiled from
          primary instruments against a published rubric. The attribution string for each appears
          on the <a href="/sources/">sources page</a> and in the marker attached to every figure
          drawn from it.
        </p>

        <h2>Material published under third-party licences</h2>
        <p>
          Most figures on this site are reproduced from third-party datasets under their own
          licences and remain the property of their publishers. Those licences are not extended by
          these terms. Check the licence on the <a href="/sources/">sources page</a>, or in the
          marker attached to the figure, before reuse.
        </p>
        <p>
          Two conditions are noted here. The AI Incident Database is licensed ODbL, which imposes
          share-alike conditions on derived databases. News headlines and extracts remain the
          property of their publishers; this site displays a headline, an extract of at most 200
          characters and a link to the original.
        </p>

        <h2>Linking and attribution</h2>
        <p>
          Linking is permitted. Figures may be quoted with attribution. The site and its data must
          not be presented as endorsed by any cited publisher. No cited publisher endorses this
          site, and several of the licences relied on state this expressly.
        </p>

        <h2>Corrections and takedowns</h2>
        <p>
          Errors may be reported through the <a href="/corrections/">corrections page</a>. Rights
          holders who wish material removed may request removal by the same route. Source data is
          held in a single registry, and removing a source removes everything derived from it.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          These terms may change. Changes are published here and the date above is updated.
          Changes affecting permitted use of the material are also listed on the
          <a href="/corrections/">corrections page</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
